# Alchemist -- single source of truth for what stays out of the repo.
#
# The rule of thumb: this repo ships the *agents* (prompts, workflows, skills,
# scripts, resources). It does not ship what those agents produce on a local
# run, or the environments they run in. Curated example outputs will be added
# back deliberately, not by accident.


# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit these. Secrets belong in the macOS Keychain.
.env
.env.*
*.secret
tokens.json
credentials.json

**/.claude/settings.local.json

# forage/.claude/settings.json holds the Globus client and collection
# UUIDs -- private infrastructure identifiers, not shareable. Cloners copy
# settings.json.example (tracked) and fill in their own.
**/.claude/settings.json
!**/.claude/settings.json.example

# Real institutional metadata: named requesters, lab names, IBC numbers and
# internal filesystem paths. resources/metadata_example.csv ships instead --
# same schema, synthetic rows -- so the mock demo runs without it.
forage/resources/metadata.csv

# Real internal project codes (SCI-######) mapped to project names -- a site's
# research portfolio. project_codes.example.json ships instead.
forage/resources/project_codes.json


# NOTE ON THE **/ PREFIX BELOW
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so a bare
# "output/*" would only match a top-level output/ and would silently miss
# brew/output/. The **/ prefix is what makes these match at any depth.
# Verify any change with:  git status --short


# --- Generated output --------------------------------------------------------
# Every agent writes its reports to output/. All of it is a local run artifact:
# dated .md/.pdf reports, plus the intermediate .html from render_report.py.
# .gitkeep preserves the directory for a fresh clone. Applies to any agent
# added later, not just the three here.
#
# EXCEPTION: a short, EXPLICIT allowlist of synthetic sample outputs, committed
# so a cloner sees the format without running anything. Each says in its own
# first line that it is synthetic.
#
# This list is deliberately not a glob. An earlier `!**/output/EXAMPLE_*`
# pattern silently un-ignored a real run that happened to be named EXAMPLE_*,
# and it carried a named requester, internal project codes and real paths.
# Outputs can hold unpublished results, so a new sample gets added here by hand
# after someone has actually read it.
**/output/*
!**/output/.gitkeep
!distill/output/EXAMPLE_research_report.md
!distill/output/EXAMPLE_research_report.pdf
!brew/output/EXAMPLE_protocol.md
!brew/output/EXAMPLE_protocol.pdf
!forage/output/EXAMPLE_discovery_report.md
!forage/output/EXAMPLE_discovery_report.pdf


# --- forage: knowledge stores ------------------------------------------
# Endpoint scan state. file_associations.jsonl is ~920 MB and inventory.jsonl
# ~436 MB -- GitHub hard-rejects anything over 100 MB, so these can never be
# tracked. The small rollups (ASSOCIATIONS.md, coverage.json, query_log.jsonl)
# are regenerable from a scan and are ignored too. The one committed sample is
# named explicitly, for the same reason as under output/.
forage/knowledge/*
!forage/knowledge/.gitkeep
!forage/knowledge/EXAMPLE_ASSOCIATIONS.md


# --- brew: downloaded data ----------------------------------------------
# Public GEO downloads plus the probe.json / samples.csv that geo_probe.py
# writes. Reproducible from the accession, and a single series can be tens of
# GB. To ship a probe as an example, add:
#   !brew/data/GSE252365/  and  !brew/data/**/probe.json
brew/data/*
!brew/data/.gitkeep

# Archives OF that directory. `brew/data/*` does not match a sibling zip, so a
# Finder "Compress" on data/ lands a tracked brew/data.zip holding exactly the
# payloads the rule above exists to exclude -- and inside an archive nobody
# reviews it, plus __MACOSX/ and .DS_Store noise.
brew/data.zip
brew/data*.zip
brew/data*.tar.gz


# --- bias reporting ----------------------------------------------------------
# Opt-in per-run influence log. It records what a run was actually about --
# queries, intake answers, and the profile facts that shaped them -- so it is
# local monitoring state, not a deliverable. config.json IS tracked: it ships
# disabled, and that default is part of the agent.
bias/log.jsonl


# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- R (brew emits .Rmd) ------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# --- macOS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
